{ Editorial study excerpt from Aman Hambleton's London series. The video handle was systemplayer; the recovered archive uses systematic. Result * marks an excerpt, not a change to the actual game result. Comments and analysis variations are editorial. https://www.chess.com/game/live/51998959937 Aman Hambleton's London System, Part 10. Verified game/review point at 8:10; this is not an exact game-start marker. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NtcXbhKBWwI&list=PLUjxDD7HNNTiljFCufDXDSjEQH1cIdbSx&t=490s } 1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 e6 4. Nd2 { Nd2 develops before Nf3. The queen still sees h5 until Ngf3 blocks the diagonal. } 4... Nh5 { After 4...Nh5?: the queen still sees h5 because the g1-knight has not gone to f3. Qxh5 wins the knight. } 5. Qxh5 Be7 6. Bd3 g6 7. Qh6 Bf6 8. Ngf3 Nc6 9. c3 Qe7 { Recorded continuation. See the complete corpus for the rest of the game and its actual result. } *

